   ◆ Ada's past: "He paid his rent regularly, and never asked for anything more than was absolutely necessary."
   ◆ Arthur's past: He was careful to keep out of debt.
   ◆ Mr. Thomas's past: He has always been a man who hated spending money unnecessarily, and was particular in never owing anybody anything.
   📅 Ada means to: Monday: washes and mends Bert's shirts, and looks over his clothes | Tuesday: clears away the week's accumulation of dust from the rooms, and sets them to rights | Wednesday: goes to the wash | Thursday: cooks and clear away, and sets the place straight again | Friday: pays the rent
   📅 Arthur means to: Monday: posts his letters, and gets in coal | Tuesday: pays his rent, and buys shoes for Joan | Wednesday: pays for the washing | Thursday: settles his book club | Friday: goes to the theatre, and have supper afterwards at a place of entertainment
   📅 Mr. Thomas means to: Monday: sees to getting in the winter's coals | Wednesday: pays the gas-bill, and looks at the state of his stock of sugar
