   ◇ Ada reflects: She thinks him a dishonest man, because he tried to cheat her out of a silver pencil worth half-a-crown.
   ◇ Ada reflects: She thinks him ungrateful, because, when he enlisted, he left her to pay the whole of the rent, and to find herself in food.
   ◇ Ada reflects: She thinks him mean, because he wanted his rent, and because he has raised it from seven shillings to eight.
   ◇ Arthur reflects: She is thrifty.
   ◇ Mr. Thomas reflects: He thinks her honest, because she told him she had found a silver pencil under a desk, and because she spoke to him about it.
   ◇ Mr. Thomas reflects: He thinks him a painstaking and trustworthy clerk, because he has never detected him in an error, and because he has always found the quarterly ledgers correct.
