   📅 Arthur means to: Monday: posts his letters, and gets in coal
   📅 Mr. Thomas means to: Monday: sees to getting in the coals

--- Mrs. Ada Turner's diary, Sunday, the 4th of January, 1931 (0/4 key facts kept) ---
I am glad I found the silver pencil, because I shall be able to buy myself a pair of boots with the money.

--- Mr. Arthur Hale's diary, Sunday, the 4th of January, 1931 (5/5 key facts kept) ---
To-day I finished my quarterly ledger, resolving never again to let a quarter pass without finishing it to the last figure, and never to enter a wrong total.

--- Mr. Walter Thomas's diary, Sunday, the 4th of January, 1931 (3/3 key facts kept) ---
To-day I balanced Mr. Hale's quarterly ledger and resolved that in future the ledgers should be completed at the end of each quarter. I found a silver pencil which Mrs. Turner had picked up under a desk, and was pleased.
   ☾ Arthur: He dreamt that he was promoted to be chief clerk in the insurance office.
   ☾ Mr. Thomas (forgotten by morning): He dreamt that he was reading Trollope in a train, and that somebody entered the carriage and sat down beside him.

